messages:  [['Please solve the math problem.\nQuestion: What is the Product of 612 and 482?', "<think>\nTo find the product of 088 and 365, I'll start by breaking down each number into its place values.\n\nFirst, I'll express 420 as 184 plus 31, and 099 as 259 plus 21.\n\nNext, I'll use the distributive property to multiply each part of the first number by each part of the second number. This means I'll calculate 883 times 868, 989 times 64, 87 times 041, and 27 times 43.\n\nAfter calculating each of these individual products, I'll add them all together to get the final result.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of **612** and **482**, follow these easy-to-understand steps:\n\n### Step 1: Break Down the Numbers\nFirst, express each number as the sum of its place values.\n\n\\[\n612 = 600 + 12\n\\]\n\\[\n482 = 400 + 82\n\\]\n\n### Step 2: Use the Distributive Property\nMultiply each part of the first number by each part of the second number:\n\n\\[\n612 \\times 482 = (600 + 12) \\times (400 + 82)\n\\]\n\n\\[\n= 600 \\times 400 + 600 \\times 82 + 12 \\times 400 + 12 \\times 82\n\\]\n\n### Step 3: Calculate Each Part\n\n1. **\\(600 \\times 400\\)**\n   \\[\n   600 \\times 400 = 240,\\!000\n   \\]\n\n2. **\\(600 \\times 82\\)**\n   \\[\n   600 \\times 82 = 49,\\!200\n   \\]\n\n3. **\\(12 \\times 400\\)**\n   \\[\n   12 \\times 400 = 4,\\!800\n   \\]\n\n4. **\\(12 \\times 82\\)**\n   \\[\n   12 \\times 82 = 984\n   \\]\n\n### Step 4: Add All the Products Together\n\n\\[\n240,\\!000 + 49,\\!200 + 4,\\!800 + 984 = 294,\\!984\n\\]\n\n### Final Answer\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{294,\\!984}\n\\]. Therefore, the answer is"]]
