messages:  [['Please solve the math problem.\nQuestion: What is the Product of 703 and 973?', "<think>\nTo find the product of 428 and 700, I'll start by breaking down each number into smaller, more manageable parts. This makes the multiplication process easier and reduces the chance of errors.\n\nFirst, I'll express 927 as 986 plus 5, and 881 as 395 plus 35. This way, I can use the distributive property to multiply each part separately.\n\nNext, I'll multiply each component of the first number by each component of the second number. This involves four separate multiplications: 643 times 321, 429 times 68, 7 times 787, and 9 times 49.\n\nAfter calculating each of these individual products, I'll add them all together to get the final result. This step-by-step approach ensures that the multiplication is accurate and straightforward.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of **703** and **973**, follow these easy-to-understand steps:\n\n### Step 1: Break Down the Numbers\nStart by expressing each number as a sum of smaller parts to make multiplication easier.\n\n\\[\n703 = 700 + 3\n\\]\n\\[\n973 = 900 + 73\n\\]\n\n### Step 2: Use the Distributive Property\nMultiply each part of the first number by each part of the second number.\n\n\\[\n703 \\times 973 = (700 + 3) \\times (900 + 73)\n\\]\n\n\\[\n= 700 \\times 900 + 700 \\times 73 + 3 \\times 900 + 3 \\times 73\n\\]\n\n### Step 3: Calculate Each Part\n\n1. **First Part:**\n\\[\n700 \\times 900 = 630,\\!000\n\\]\n\n2. **Second Part:**\n\\[\n700 \\times 73 = 51,\\!100\n\\]\n\n3. **Third Part:**\n\\[\n3 \\times 900 = 2,\\!700\n\\]\n\n4. **Fourth Part:**\n\\[\n3 \\times 73 = 219\n\\]\n\n### Step 4: Add All the Parts Together\n\n\\[\n630,\\!000 + 51,\\!100 + 2,\\!700 + 219 = 683,\\!019\n\\]\n\n### Final Answer\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{683,\\!019}\n\\]. Therefore, the answer is"]]
