messages:  [['Please solve the math problem.\nQuestion: What is the Product of 260 and 305?', "<think>\nTo find the product of 547 and 647, I'll start by breaking down each number into its place values.\n\nFirst, I'll express 783 as 428 plus 03, and 128 as 075 plus 7.\n\nNext, I'll use the distributive property to multiply each part of 815 by each part of 712.\n\nThis will give me four separate multiplication problems: 729 times 974, 793 times 7, 09 times 255, and 46 times 2.\n\nAfter calculating each of these, I'll add all the results together to find the final product.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of **260** and **305**, follow these easy steps:\n\n### Step 1: Break Down the Numbers\nFirst, express each number as the sum of its place values.\n\n\\[\n260 = 200 + 60\n\\]\n\\[\n305 = 300 + 5\n\\]\n\n### Step 2: Use the Distributive Property\nMultiply each part of the first number by each part of the second number:\n\n\\[\n260 \\times 305 = (200 + 60) \\times (300 + 5)\n\\]\n\n\\[\n= 200 \\times 300 + 200 \\times 5 + 60 \\times 300 + 60 \\times 5\n\\]\n\n### Step 3: Calculate Each Part\n\n1. **\\(200 \\times 300\\)**\n   \\[\n   200 \\times 300 = 60,\\!000\n   \\]\n\n2. **\\(200 \\times 5\\)**\n   \\[\n   200 \\times 5 = 1,\\!000\n   \\]\n\n3. **\\(60 \\times 300\\)**\n   \\[\n   60 \\times 300 = 18,\\!000\n   \\]\n\n4. **\\(60 \\times 5\\)**\n   \\[\n   60 \\times 5 = 300\n   \\]\n\n### Step 4: Add All the Results Together\n\n\\[\n60,\\!000 + 1,\\!000 + 18,\\!000 + 300 = 79,\\!300\n\\]\n\n### Final Answer\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{79,\\!300}\n\\]. Therefore, the answer is"]]
