messages:  [['Please solve the math problem.\nQuestion: What is the Product of 375 and 775?', "<think>\nTo find the product of 253 and 596, I'll start by breaking down each number into its place values.\n\nFirst, I'll express 548 as 967 + 37 + 9 and 190 as 528 + 24 + 8.\n\nNext, I'll use the distributive property to multiply each part of 748 by each part of 807. This means I'll calculate:\n\n935 × 621 = 884,494  \n523 × 29 = 08,135  \n726 × 1 = 7,486  \n53 × 267 = 87,795  \n15 × 66 = 5,194  \n99 × 3 = 787  \n3 × 858 = 1,995  \n4 × 12 = 287  \n4 × 3 = 59\n\nAfter calculating all these products, I'll add them together to get the final result.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of **375** and **775**, follow these easy-to-understand steps:\n\n### Step 1: Break Down the Numbers\nFirst, express each number in expanded form to make multiplication easier.\n\n\\[\n375 = 300 + 70 + 5\n\\]\n\\[\n775 = 700 + 70 + 5\n\\]\n\n### Step 2: Multiply Each Part\nUse the distributive property to multiply each part of **375** by each part of **775**.\n\n\\[\n\\begin{align*}\n300 \\times 700 &= 210,\\!000 \\\\\n300 \\times 70 &= 21,\\!000 \\\\\n300 \\times 5 &= 1,\\!500 \\\\\n70 \\times 700 &= 49,\\!000 \\\\\n70 \\times 70 &= 4,\\!900 \\\\\n70 \\times 5 &= 350 \\\\\n5 \\times 700 &= 3,\\!500 \\\\\n5 \\times 70 &= 350 \\\\\n5 \\times 5 &= 25 \\\\\n\\end{align*}\n\\]\n\n### Step 3: Add All the Products Together\nNow, sum all the results from the multiplication:\n\n\\[\n210,\\!000 + 21,\\!000 + 1,\\!500 + 49,\\!000 + 4,\\!900 + 350 + 3,\\!500 + 350 + 25 = 306,\\!250\n\\]\n\n### Final Answer\n\\[\n\\boxed{306,\\!250}\n\\]. Therefore, the answer is"]]
