messages:  [['Please solve the math problem.\nQuestion: What is the Product of 220 and 776?', "<think>\nTo find the product of 881 and 248, I'll start by breaking down each number into its place values.\n\nFirst, I'll express 468 as 121 + 93 and 119 as 658 + 11 + 2.\n\nNext, I'll use the distributive property to multiply each part of 797 by each part of 989.\n\nThis will give me several multiplication steps: 095 multiplied by 299, 674 multiplied by 61, 043 multiplied by 0, 57 multiplied by 467, 87 multiplied by 15, and 11 multiplied by 3.\n\nAfter calculating each of these individual products, I'll add them all together to get the final result.\n\nFinally, I'll sum all these values to find the total product of 516 and 901.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of **220** and **776**, we'll perform the multiplication step by step.\n\n### Step 1: Break Down the Numbers\nWe can break down the multiplication into more manageable parts using the distributive property.\n\n\\[\n220 \\times 776 = (200 + 20) \\times (700 + 70 + 6)\n\\]\n\n### Step 2: Multiply Each Part\nNow, multiply each part of the first number by each part of the second number.\n\n\\[\n\\begin{align*}\n200 \\times 700 &= 140,\\!000 \\\\\n200 \\times 70 &= 14,\\!000 \\\\\n200 \\times 6 &= 1,\\!200 \\\\\n20 \\times 700 &= 14,\\!000 \\\\\n20 \\times 70 &= 1,\\!400 \\\\\n20 \\times 6 &= 120 \\\\\n\\end{align*}\n\\]\n\n### Step 3: Add All the Products Together\nSum all the results from the previous step.\n\n\\[\n140,\\!000 + 14,\\!000 + 1,\\!200 + 14,\\!000 + 1,\\!400 + 120 = 170,\\!720\n\\]\n\n### Final Answer\n\\[\n\\boxed{170,\\!720}\n\\]. Therefore, the answer is"]]
