messages:   59%|#####8    | 294/500 [07:36<00:29,  6.92it/s][['Please solve the math problem.\nQuestion: What is the Product of 903 and 732?', "<think>\nTo find the product of 156 and 203, I'll start by breaking down each number into its place values.\n\nFirst, I'll express 338 as 351 plus 8, and 124 as 483 plus 85.\n\nNext, I'll use the distributive property to multiply each part of 381 by each part of 604.\n\nThis will give me four separate multiplication problems: 465 multiplied by 522, 563 multiplied by 77, 1 multiplied by 676, and 7 multiplied by 15.\n\nAfter calculating each of these individual products, I'll add them all together to get the final result.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of **903** and **732**, follow these easy-to-understand steps:\n\n### Step 1: Break Down the Numbers\nFirst, express each number as the sum of its place values.\n\n\\[\n903 = 900 + 3\n\\]\n\\[\n732 = 700 + 32\n\\]\n\n### Step 2: Use the Distributive Property\nMultiply each part of the first number by each part of the second number.\n\n\\[\n903 \\times 732 = (900 + 3) \\times (700 + 32)\n\\]\n\n\\[\n= 900 \\times 700 + 900 \\times 32 + 3 \\times 700 + 3 \\times 32\n\\]\n\n### Step 3: Calculate Each Part\n\n1. **Multiply 900 by 700:**\n   \\[\n   900 \\times 700 = 630,\\!000\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 900 by 32:**\n   \\[\n   900 \\times 32 = 28,\\!800\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 3 by 700:**\n   \\[\n   3 \\times 700 = 2,\\!100\n   \\]\n\n4. **Multiply 3 by 32:**\n   \\[\n   3 \\times 32 = 96\n   \\]\n\n### Step 4: Add All the Products Together\n\n\\[\n630,\\!000 + 28,\\!800 + 2,\\!100 + 96 = 661,\\!000 - 4 (Adjusting for the exact sum)\n\\]\n\n\\[\n= 661,\\!000 - 4 = 660,\\!996\n\\]\n\n### Final Answer\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{660,\\!996}\n\\]. Therefore, the answer is"]]
