messages:  [['Please solve the math problem.\nQuestion: What is the Product of 851 and 816?', "<think>\nTo find the product of 415 and 943, I'll start by breaking down each number into smaller, more manageable parts using the distributive property.\n\nFirst, I'll express 406 as 453 plus 11 plus 2. Similarly, I'll express 143 as 273 plus 09.\n\nNext, I'll multiply each part of the first number by each part of the second number. This involves calculating eight separate products: 453 times 147, 755 times 22, 21 times 098, 48 times 53, 2 times 745, 4 times 88, and so on.\n\nAfter calculating all these individual products, I'll add them all together to get the final result. This step-by-step approach ensures that I don't miss any components and helps in accurately computing the total product.\n</think>.\n\nTo find the product of **851** and **816**, we'll use the **standard multiplication algorithm**. Here's a step-by-step solution:.\n\n### Step 1: Write the Numbers Vertically.\n\n```.\n   851.\n×  816.\n--------.\n```.\n\n### Step 2: Multiply 851 by Each Digit of 816.\n\n1. **Multiply by 6 (units place):**.\n   \\[.\n   851 \\times 6 = 5106.\n   \\].\n   .\n2. **Multiply by 10 (tens place):**.\n   \\[.\n   851 \\times 10 = 8510 \\quad (\\text{Shift one position to the left}).\n   \\].\n   .\n3. **Multiply by 800 (hundreds place):**.\n   \\[.\n   851 \\times 800 = 680800 \\quad (\\text{Shift two positions to the left}).\n   \\].\n\n### Step 3: Add All the Products Together.\n\n\\[.\n\\begin{align*}.\n& \\quad \\,\\,\\, 5106 \\\\.\n& + \\,\\, 85100 \\\\.\n& + 680800 \\\\.\n\\hline. Therefore, the answer is"]]
