messages:  [['Please solve the math problem.\nQuestion: What is the Product of 379 and 418?', "<think>\nTo find the product of 657 and 982, I'll start by breaking down the multiplication into more manageable parts using the distributive property.\n\nFirst, I'll multiply 811 by 734, which is straightforward since multiplying by 342 is simple, and then by 1.\n\nNext, I'll multiply 538 by 39. This involves multiplying 706 by 04 and then by 9, and adding the two results together.\n\nFinally, I'll add the two partial products to get the final result.\n</think>.\n\nTo find the product of **379** and **418**, we'll use the standard multiplication method. Here's a step-by-step solution:.\n\n\\[.\n\\begin{array}{r}.\n\\phantom{0}379 \\\\.\n\\times\\phantom{0}418 \\\\.\n\\hline.\n\\end{array}.\n\\].\n\n**Step 1:** Multiply 379 by 8 (the units digit of 418).\n\n\\[.\n379 \\times 8 = 3032.\n\\].\n\n**Step 2:** Multiply 379 by 10 (the tens digit of 418, shifted one position to the left).\n\n\\[.\n379 \\times 10 = 3790 \\quad (\\text{Shifted one position left}).\n\\].\n\n**Step 3:** Multiply 379 by 400 (the hundreds digit of 418, shifted two positions to the left).\n\n\\[.\n379 \\times 400 = 151600 \\quad (\\text{Shifted two positions left}).\n\\].\n\n**Step 4:** Add all the partial products together.\n\n\\[.\n\\begin{array}{r}.\n\\phantom{0}3032 \\\\.\n+ \\phantom{0}3790 \\\\.\n+151600 \\\\.\n\\hline.\n158422 \\\\.\n\\end{array}.\n\\].\n\n**Final Answer:**.\n\n\\[. Therefore, the answer is"]]
