messages:  [['Please solve the math problem.\nQuestion: What is the Product of 684 and 486?', "<think>\nTo find the product of 977 and 219, I'll start by breaking down each number into its place values. \n\nFirst, I'll express 560 as 436 + 99 + 9 and 105 as 017 + 14 + 4. \n\nNext, I'll use the distributive property to multiply each part of the first number by each part of the second number. This means I'll calculate 741 multiplied by 241, 739 multiplied by 15, 345 multiplied by 2, and so on for each component.\n\nAfter calculating all these individual products, I'll add them all together to get the final result. This step-by-step approach ensures that I don't miss any part of the multiplication and helps in keeping track of the calculations accurately.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of **684** and **486**, we'll use the standard multiplication method. Here's a step-by-step solution:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{array}{r}\n\\phantom{0}684 \\\\\n\\times 486 \\\\\n\\hline\n\\end{array}\n\\]\n\n**Step 1: Multiply 684 by 6 (units place of 486)**\n\n\\[\n684 \\times 6 = 4104\n\\]\n\n**Step 2: Multiply 684 by 80 (tens place of 486)**\n\n\\[\n684 \\times 80 = 54,\\!720\n\\]\n\n**Step 3: Multiply 684 by 400 (hundreds place of 486)**\n\n\\[\n684 \\times 400 = 273,\\!600\n\\]\n\n**Step 4: Add all the results together**\n\n\\[\n\\begin{array}{r}\n\\phantom{0}4104 \\\\\n+54,\\!720 \\\\\n+273,\\!600 \\\\\n\\hline\n332,\\!424 \\\\\n\\end{array}\n\\]\n\n**Final Answer:**\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{332,\\!424}\n\\]. Therefore, the answer is"]]
