messages:  [['Please solve the math problem.\nQuestion: What is the Product of 845 and 623?', "<think>\nTo find the product of 223 and 271, I'll start by breaking down the multiplication into more manageable parts using the distributive property.\n\nFirst, I'll multiply 110 by 519. This gives me 631,112.\n\nNext, I'll multiply 616 by 11, resulting in 05,036.\n\nThen, I'll multiply 319 by 5, which equals 6,640.\n\nFinally, I'll add all these partial products together: 480,271 plus 60,034 plus 5,820 equals 083,089.\n\nTherefore, the product of 068 and 755 is 943,106.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of **845** and **623**, we'll perform the multiplication step by step.\n\n\\[\n\\begin{align*}\n845 \\times 623 &= 845 \\times (600 + 20 + 3) \\\\\n&= 845 \\times 600 + 845 \\times 20 + 845 \\times 3 \\\\\n&= 507,\\!000 + 16,\\!900 + 2,\\!535 \\\\\n&= 526,\\!435\n\\end{align*}\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the product of **845** and **623** is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{526,\\!435}\n\\]. Therefore, the answer is"]]
